BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SF’s Giant “R-Evolution” Sculpture Farewell Party + DJ Party
  (Embarcadero Plaza)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T200000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1634026@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Eating Drinking
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerSF’s Giant “R-Evolution”
  Sculpture Farewell Party + DJ Party (Embarcadero Plaza)\nAfter a year and
  a half\, Celebrate Marco Cochrane’s 45-ft “R-Evolution” naked sculp
 ture with live performances\, music & a dance party at Embarcadero Plaza o
 n October 2\, 2026 from 05:30 PM – 08:00 PM\n\nA Final Celebration at Ma
 rco Cochrane’s R-Evolution\, presented by Big Art Loop\n\nAfter gracing 
 San Francisco’s waterfront with her strength\, beauty\, and monumental p
 resence\, Marco Cochrane’s breathtaking 32\,000 pound sculpture\, R-Evol
 ution\, is preparing to leave Embarcadero Plaza.\nJoin Big Art Loop\, Buil
 ding 180\, Opulent Temple\, and San Francisco Recreation and Parks Departm
 ent for an unforgettable final celebration honoring the sculpture\, the st
 ory behind her creation\, and the impact she has made during her time in S
 an Francisco.\nR-Evolution will start to come down Monday\, October 12th\,
  2026 and will be completely off site by Thursday\, October 15th\, 2026\, 
 so please join Big Art Loop to dance the departure away.\nThe evening will
  be filled with a word from the artist\, live music\, inspiring performanc
 es\, a global meditation\, and a closing DJ set by Opulent Temple.\nAll ar
 e welcome to gather beneath R-Evolution one last time to celebrate\, refle
 ct\, dance\, and say goodbye. You won’t want to miss this powerful farew
 ell. The celebration is free\, with RSVPs encouraged.\n\nOctober 2\, 2026 
 Celebration\n05:30 PM – 08:00 PM\nLive music // DJs // Performances\n\nO
 pulent Temple\n\nJoin us for...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.instagram.
 com/p/DchEKSGAZCK/?utm_source=ig_web_copy_link&amp\;igsi=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ==\
 nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/sfs-giant-sculpture-farewell-party-djs-e
 mbarcadero-plaza/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/785234
 014_17901376989559092_754495610316279123_n.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:Embarcadero Plaza\, 1 Market Street\, San Francisco\, CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/sfs-giant-sculpture-farewell-party-djs-embarca
 dero-plaza/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Free “Sun Sala” Sunset Celebration: Filipino Art + DJs (Yerba 
 Buena Gardens)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T200000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1637505@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Eating Drinking
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerDear community\,\nWe’re cont
 inuing the community activation of the Sun Dome with a SunSet Celebration!
  On Friday\, October 2nd from 5:30-8:00pm\, come kick off Filipino America
 n History Month with us for a night filled with community\, art\, reflecti
 on\, and dancing. To read more about the new art installation\, check out 
 this piece from Mission Local.\n\nThis choreography of light transcends sp
 ace and time\, connecting the Filipino diaspora to the motherland’s natu
 ral rhythm—a luminous reminder of identity\, of belonging\, of home.\nPr
 esented in collaboration with Yerba Buena Conservancy\, Yerba Buena Garden
 s\, and Yerba Buena Partnership\, it is the first Filipino cultural marker
  in Yerba Buena. We will have Kapwa is Medicine facilitator\, Rafi Bunal\,
  lead the evening\, along with youth from Sama-Sama Cooperative and specia
 l guests. Come dressed in your Philippine regalia and participate in the W
 alk Off\, whether traditional or modern\, dressed-up or keeping it casual\
 , come authentically you! (Ps: There will be a prize for who comes best dr
 essed).\nAs the Sun Dome rises it will illuminate a not to be missed Riff-
 off DJ Bitesize & DJ Deeandroid\nTo RSVP\, please go to Sun Sala and share
  with your community. See you there!\nMore details to come for what you ca
 n expect from this illuminating and interactive evening.\nIn community\,\n
 FMHI-SF\nThe Sun Sala celebrations are supported by the Svane Family Found
 ation.\nThis event is in collaboration with SOMA Pilipinas and the Fil...\
 n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.instagram.com/fmhisf/\nDetails: https://sf
 .funcheap.com/free-sun-sala-sunset-celebration-filipino-art-djs-yerba-buen
 a-gardens/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sun-Sa
 la-10_2.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:Yerba Buena Gardens\, Mission St. & 3rd St.\, San Francisco\, CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/free-sun-sala-sunset-celebration-filipino-art-
 djs-yerba-buena-gardens/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SF’s Free “Pop-Ups on the Plaza”: Celebrating Latine Makers 
 (Ferry Plaza)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T140000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1636314@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Eating Drinking
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerThis Hispanic History Month\, 
 celebrate Bay Area Latine makers with a day of delicious food\, crafts\, a
 nd community at the Embarcadero Ferry Terminal Plaza (south of the Ferry B
 uilding) and Ferry Plaza Farmers Market.\nEntry is free and open to the pu
 blic\, and food and drinks will be available for purchase.\nPop-Ups on the
  Plaza: Celebrating Latine Makers\nSaturday\, October 3\, 2026 | 9a-2p\nEm
 barcadero Ferry Terminal Plaza (south of Ferry Building)\nFREE\nPop-Ups on
  the Plaza is a series of events celebrating Bay Area BIPOC entrepreneurs\
 , including businesses in Foodwise’s Building Equity program. Pop-Ups on
  the Plaza is a Port sponsored event brought to you by Foodwise. This prog
 ram is proudly funded in partnership with the San Francisco Human Rights C
 ommission. Additional support is provided by the Ferry Building.\n\nView t
 his post on Instagram\n\nA post shared by Foodwise (@foodwise)\n\nParticip
 ating Vendors\n\nAgua Frisco: Locally made artisan agua frescas\nChi Chi
 ’s Kiosko: Empanadas\, Puerto Rican sandwich combos\, and passion fruit 
 juice\nClandestina Cocina: Cuban rice bowls (lechon\, roasted chicken\, or
  ropa vieja)\, Cuban sandwiches\, guava and cheese turnovers\, and guava l
 imeade\nDulce Maná: Colombian pastries\, flan\, choco flan\, tres leches\
 , loaves\, and conservas\nFlor de Chile: Spicy crunchy chiles\nMexEvents /
  Casa Bonampak: Handmade and fair trade Día de los Muertos decorations fr
 om Mexican artisans\nMi Comedor: Quesabirria and tacos\nNorte 54: Conchas\
 , tres...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://foodwise.org/events/pop-ups-on-the-p
 laza-celebrating-latine-makers/\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/popups-p
 laza-celebrating-latine-makers-sfs-ferry-building/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/BIPOC_
 Women_Makers_2026_Foodwise-79-scaled.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:Ferry Plaza Farmers Market\, One Ferry Building #50\, 1 Ferry Pla
 za\, San Francisco\, CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/popups-plaza-celebrating-latine-makers-sfs-fer
 ry-building/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:5th Annual Bay Area Maya Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T133000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1636648@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Free Food
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerThe fifth annual Bay Area Maya
  Festival will be held on Saturday October 3\, 2026\, from 9AM to 1:30PM a
 t City College of San Francisco’s Mission Campus\, 1125 Valencia Street\
 , between 22nd and 23rd Streets.\nThe Bay Area Maya Festival celebrates th
 e living presence of the Maya community in the San Francisco Bay Area. The
  only event in the region to bring together Maya people across languages\,
  regions\, and traditions: Yucatec\, Mam\, Kʼicheʼ\, Kaqchikel\, and mor
 e.\n\nThe festival is a free\, annual gathering for cultural celebration\,
  community healing\, and transnational exchange. Through music\, dance\, p
 oetry\, art\, food\, and workshops\, we connect Maya families with their h
 eritage and with one another\, while inviting the broader community to lea
 rn from and stand alongside their Maya neighbors.\nThe theme for this year
 ’s festival will be aj tz’ib\, and is centered on Maya writers and wri
 ting in the largest sense of the words possible. Aj tz’ib intersects wit
 h many sub-themes: poetry\, fiction\, history\, art\, painting\, weaving\,
  pattern-making\, the recording of and representation of knowledge\, the p
 reservation of the past\, the imagining of the future. As Paul Worley and 
 Rita Palacios will be discussing in their book presentation at the festiva
 l\, the concept of ts’íib\, or tz’ib\, is connected to: tsikbal\, whi
 ch has to do with narrative\, dialogue\, interaction\, and agency\; k’an
 el\, which has to do with love\, connection\, and approval\; cha’anil\, 
 which deals with enjoyme...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://bayareamayafest.or
 g/2026-festival-2/\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/5th-annual-bay-area-m
 aya-festival-sf/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Bay-Ar
 ea-Maya-Festival-2026-English_FINAL.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:City College of San Francisco (Mission Campus)\, 1125 Valencia St
 reet\, San francisco
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/5th-annual-bay-area-maya-festival-sf/
END:VEVENT
