DESCRIPTION:rafikiThe 2026 election is closer than it feels\, and the deci
 sions on the ballot will shape health\, housing\, food access\, and safety
  net programs for Black San Franciscans for years to come.\nJoin us for AA
 CHEC’s Fall Civic Engagement Teach-In Series: a nonpartisan\, community-
 centered conversation about what’s changing and what it means for you.\n
 We’ll break down — in plain language — what’s on the ballot\, what
 ’s shifting in Medi-Cal\, CalFresh\, and federal housing programs\, and 
 what community members can do right now to make their voices heard.\n\nThi
 s isn’t a campaign event. It’s information you need\, from people you 
 trust.\nWhat we’ll cover:\n\nKey ballot measures in the November 2026 el
 ection\nRecent and pending changes to Medi-Cal and Medicaid\nSNAP and CalF
 resh: what’s at stake for food access\nHousing and safety-net policy shi
 fts at the local\, state\, and federal level\nHow to connect with Black he
 alth equity advocacy in San Francisco\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.even
 tbrite.com/e/aachec-san-francisco-community-teach-in-tickets-2002677884463
 \nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/whats-stake-free-2026-ballot-breakdown-
 sf-lgbt-center/\nSource: Funcheap SF
