DESCRIPTION:Italian Heritage Festival & ParadeThe San Francisco Italian He
 ritage Parade returns to the streets of San Francisco on Sunday\, October 
 11\, 2026\, bringing Italian-American culture\, music\, performances\, flo
 ats\, and community groups to the streets of North Beach.\nThe San Francis
 co Italian Heritage Parade is the longest continuously running Italian Her
 itage Parade in the United States and celebrates the accomplishments and c
 ulture of Italian-Americans. The inaugural parade took place in 1868 in do
 wntown San Francisco\, featuring bands and marching units from Italian fra
 ternal organizations. Throughout the years\, the parade has remained a cel
 ebration of the vitality of Italian communities throughout the Bay Area.\n
 Parade Route\nThe parade begins at 12:30 p.m. at the foot of Jefferson and
  Powell Streets in Fisherman’s Wharf\, then proceeds through North Beach
  along Columbus Avenue before ending in Washington Square in front of Sain
 ts Peter and Paul Church. Parade viewing is available throughout the entir
 e route.\n\nThe celebration features Italian and Italian-American dignitar
 ies\, live Italian music\, performances\, floats\, and representatives fro
 m Italian and Italian-American organizations and businesses. Admission is 
 free.\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://sfitalianheritage.org/\nDetails: https:/
 /sf.funcheap.com/san-francisco-italian-heritage-parade-festival/\nSource: 
 Funcheap SF
