DESCRIPTION:“Pay-What-You-Can” Taco Day at SF’s Tato (Every Friday)\
 nTATO\nWhile many restaurants are struggling\, San Francisco Mexican resta
 urant TATO wants to give back.\nThey’re bringing back their “Taco Love
 ” special which features a two taco plate with sides\, and pay-what-you-
 can pricing.\nPay-What-You-Can Taco Day\nTato\n4608 3rd St. (@ McKinnon) S
 an Francisco (Bayview)\nEvery Friday from 11am to 5 pm\, customers can ord
 er off the Taco Love menu and pay anywhere from $0 up to $10. When a custo
 mer pays the full price of $10\, TATO will give a free meal to someone in 
 need in The City.\nClosed Christmas & New Years / Restarting January 8\, 2
 021 – Tato plans to offer Taco Love “indefinitely every Friday\,” bu
 tplease check Facebook for updates as schedules can change.\n\nThe special
  is open to anyone\, but especially for fellow restaurant and bar industry
  workers who have been hit particularly hard during the pandemic.\nThe men
 u might change weekly\, but often includes Beef Quesabirria\, Mushroom Que
 sabirria\, and Chicken Tacos\n\nView this post on Instagram\n\nA post shar
